From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:27:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: pmic: mtk-pwrap: match any of the PMIC compatibles

mtk_pwrap_find_slave() compared only the first string of the PMIC
node's compatible list against the known PMICs, so PMICs described with
a specific compatible plus a fallback were not found, eg. the MT6365 on
Genio 1200 boards (MT8395 EVK, Radxa NIO-12L):

  compatible = "mediatek,mt6365", "mediatek,mt6359";

causing the wrapper probe to fail with "pmic slave not found", and in
turn everything depending on the PMIC (eg. its regulators).

Use ofnode_device_is_compatible(), which checks every compatible string,
as the driver already does elsewhere.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
---
 drivers/power/pmic/mtk-pwrap.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/pmic/mtk-pwrap.c b/drivers/power/pmic/mtk-pwrap.c
index 468af1fba04..54114608553 100644
--- a/drivers/power/pmic/mtk-pwrap.c
+++ b/drivers/power/pmic/mtk-pwrap.c
@@ -683,16 +683,15 @@ static const struct udevice_id mtk_pmic_ids[] = {
 static int mtk_pwrap_find_slave(const struct pwrap_slv_type **slave, ofnode pmic_node)
 {
 	const struct udevice_id *of_match = mtk_pmic_ids;
-	const char *pmic_name;
 
-	pmic_name = ofnode_get_property(pmic_node, "compatible", NULL);
-	if (!pmic_name) {
+	if (!ofnode_has_property(pmic_node, "compatible")) {
 		log_err("%s: missing compatible property\n", __func__);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/* Match any compatible, eg. "mediatek,mt6365", "mediatek,mt6359" */
 	while (of_match->compatible) {
-		if (!strcmp(of_match->compatible, pmic_name)) {
+		if (ofnode_device_is_compatible(pmic_node, of_match->compatible)) {
 			*slave = (struct pwrap_slv_type *)of_match->data;
 			return 0;
 		}
